meta {
  name: Partial Prefix Search (cos)
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/places?lat=37.7749&lng=-122.4194&q=cos
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  lat: 37.7749
  lng: -122.4194
  q: cos
}

docs {
  Regression case for a bug where `q=cos` returned "Cos Bar San Francisco"
  but not "Costco" -- the old Google searchText endpoint only matched whole
  tokens. The database search matches substrings through the trigram index,
  so expect both, with the word-start matches ("Cos Bar", "Costco") ahead of
  interior ones ("Tacos").
}
